==Trivia==
*Sinner Snache's Japanese name, Infernyoro (インフェルにょろ ''Inferunyoro''), is a portmanteau of ''inferno'' and にょろ ''Nyoro'' ([[Snache]]'s Japanese name).
**''Nyoro'' is another name for a wave dash (〜) or tilde (~), which Snache and its variants are vaguely shaped like.
*As a snake with a flame on its head, Sinner Snache may have been inspired by the [[wikipedia:Oxyrhopus petolarius|forest flame snake]] or fiery snakes in mythology and religion, such as the [[wikipedia:Fiery flying serpent|fiery flying serpent]], [[wikipedia:Boitatá|Boitatá]], or [[wikipedia:Xiuhcōātl|Xiuhcōātl]]. Its flame's blue coloration may reference:
**The [[wikipedia:Firedrake (folklore)|firedrake]], a type of demon from Russian folklore said to appear as a glowing ball of blue fire in East Slavic tradition.
**Chapters 14 and 19-21 of the Book of Revelation, wherein Satan and the ungodly are cast into a lake of [[wikipedia:Fire and brimstone|fire and brimstone]]; brimstone is another name for sulfur, a chemical element that burns with a blue flame.
**[[wikia:disney:Hades|Hades]] from Disney's ''[[wikipedia:Hercules (franchise)|Hercules]]'', whose hair is made up of blue fire.
*Sinner Snache's [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] trait may be a reference to how snakes are commonly associated with the Devil, the underworld, evil and deceit, such as the deceitful serpent in the [[wikipedia:Garden of Eden|Garden of Eden]].
*As with many of Snache's variants, Sinner Snache's description breaks the 4th wall, claiming water is its weakness while it has no actual in-game effect.
*Since its [[Death Surge]] only has a 50% chance of activation, Sinner Snache can have two different death animations depending on whether Death Surge activates or not.
*Sinner Snache, [[Condemned Peng]], [[Le'Behemoth]], [[Fallen Bear]] and [[Wicked Face]] were added to the game files in [[Version 10.8 Update|Version 10.8]], but were unimplemented and used [[Doge]]'s stats and sprites as placeholders until [[Version 10.9 Update|Version 10.9]].

